=== select_sweep_scope: which logs the boundary re-executes ===
  FULL rule fired / before ASSAY, NYQUIST or DONE
    touched=['src/alpha.py']
    scope=['casting-1-alpha.log', 'casting-2-beta.log', 'wave-report-sections.log']
  DELTA, diff touches casting 1's key_files
    touched=['src/alpha.py']
    scope=['casting-1-alpha.log']
  DELTA, diff touches casting 2's key_files
    touched=['src/beta.py']
    scope=['casting-2-beta.log']
  DELTA, diff touches a file under casting 3's key_files DIRECTORY
    touched=['tests/fixtures/gamma/rows.json']
    scope=['wave-report-sections.log']
  DELTA, diff touches nothing any casting or command names
    touched=['docs/README.md']
    scope=[]
=== the empty DELTA scope costs no worktree and no subprocess ===
    ok=True  scope_count=0  logs_reexecuted=[]
    head_commit=None  pool_size=0
=== a FULL sweep re-executes the whole committed corpus at HEAD ===
    ok=True  scope_count=3
    reexecuted evidence/casting-1-alpha.log
    reexecuted evidence/casting-2-beta.log
    reexecuted evidence/wave-report-sections.log
    mismatches=[]
